DYN={
'PYKT_TEXT':"""With pyKT's code, DKT reproduces its published value closely: {pk_statics2011_dkt} against {pk_statics2011_dkt_pub} on Statics 2011 and {pk_assist2015_dkt} against {pk_assist2015_dkt_pub} on ASSISTments 2015. SAKT ({pk_statics2011_sakt} against {pk_statics2011_sakt_pub}) and simpleKT ({pk_statics2011_simplekt} against {pk_statics2011_simplekt_pub}) fall short on Statics 2011, which we attribute to the missing search, since both are sensitive to learning rate and depth. The probe reaches {pk_statics2011_fkg_support} with the support graph and {pk_statics2011_fkg_empty} with the empty graph on Statics 2011. That places it above the published DKT and simpleKT and below the published AKT ({pk_statics2011_akt_pub}), which uses question-difference embeddings the probe does not have. On ASSISTments 2015 it reaches {pk_assist2015_fkg_support}, level with the published AKT ({pk_assist2015_akt_pub}). The comparison that matters for this paper is the paired one. Under the pyKT split the support graph adds {pk_statics2011_support_empty} AUC over the empty control on Statics 2011 ({pk_statics2011_support_empty_pos} of {pk_statics2011_support_empty_n} folds) and {pk_assist2015_support_empty} on ASSISTments 2015 ({pk_assist2015_support_empty_pos} of {pk_assist2015_support_empty_n} folds). Our own protocol gave {full_sup_statics11} and {full_sup_assist15} for the same two corpora with all training learners (Section 6.2). The protocol changes the absolute numbers, not the graph effect: a small gain where data per KC are scarce (Statics 2011, 1,223 KCs for about 210 training learners per fold) and none where they are plentiful (ASSISTments 2015, 100 KCs).""",
'PYKT_RESP':"""Kết quả: DKT chạy bằng mã pyKT tái lập sát số công bố ({pk_statics2011_dkt} so với {pk_statics2011_dkt_pub} trên Statics; {pk_assist2015_dkt} so với {pk_assist2015_dkt_pub} trên ASSISTments 2015). SAKT và simpleKT thấp hơn số công bố do không tìm siêu tham số. FKG-KT đạt {pk_statics2011_fkg_support} trên Statics, cao hơn DKT và simpleKT công bố, thấp hơn AKT công bố ({pk_statics2011_akt_pub}). Hiệu ứng đồ thị (support − rỗng, ghép theo fold): {pk_statics2011_support_empty} trên Statics ({pk_statics2011_support_empty_pos}/{pk_statics2011_support_empty_n} fold) và {pk_assist2015_support_empty} trên ASSISTments 2015 ({pk_assist2015_support_empty_pos}/{pk_assist2015_support_empty_n} fold), khớp với giao thức của bài ({full_sup_statics11} và {full_sup_assist15} ở 100%). ASSISTments 2015 chỉ chạy 3/5 fold vì mỗi lần huấn luyện mất 25–40 phút trên CPU. | 6.7, Bảng 6, 7.3""",

'POOLED':"""Against the empty-graph control, the pooled-cohort graph gives {pool05a} at 5% ({pool05a_pos} of 10 corpora), {pool10a} at 10% and {pool25a} at 25%, and on first attempts {pool05n}, {pool10n} and {pool25n}. Against the subsample's own graph, which it contains several times over in edges, it changes AUC by {poolsup05a} at 5% ({poolsup05a_pos} of 10 corpora higher), {poolsup10a} at 10% ({poolsup10a_pos} of 10) and {poolsup25a} at 25% ({poolsup25a_pos} of 10, Holm p = {poolsup25a_ph}); first-attempt AUC changes by {poolsup05n}, {poolsup10n} and {poolsup25n}. The larger graph is no better and, at 25%, slightly worse than the graph built from the tracer's own learners.""",
'FULLCMP':"""With all training learners the margins shrink to {cmp100_support_DKT} over DKT ({cmp100_support_DKT_pos} of {cmp100_support_DKT_n} corpora), {cmp100_support_AKT} over AKT ({cmp100_support_AKT_pos} of {cmp100_support_AKT_n}) and {cmp100_support_GKT} over GKT ({cmp100_support_GKT_pos} of {cmp100_support_GKT_n}).""",
}
